{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The run closes here with no further artifact, because everything completable is complete and the remaining minutes cannot support an experiment plus its interpretation: all fourteen registered questions are answered, there are no outstanding gaps or uncited executions, and the file I reference is the last accepted one. What this session established, each with retained receipts, declared comparisons, witnesses and explicit scope: first, with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and a commit-tracking store, NewRaft replays committed entries through a blocking send on the 128-slot FSM channel before it starts the FSM goroutine and before it returns a handle, so a replay window above 128 batches (8192 FSM-bound entries at the default batch size) leaves the constructor unable to complete - shown at the boundary, under the captured default snapshot settings, with the blocked stack in the replay path. Second, verifyLeader counts acknowledgements from every registered replication peer, nonvoters included, against a quorum that counts only voters, so a leader whose only reachable peer is a nonvoter is confirmed against a voter quorum; over twenty per-node-timer trials that confirmation outlived a competing leader's election every time and coincided with a commit index above the confirming leader's applied index in twelve of twelve, while uniform configurations kept the separation down to a one-millisecond margin, with the separating gate identified as the peers' refusal to vote while they still have the leader in view. Third, AddVoter installs the requested server as a Voter in one step against two published descriptions that promise staging, so adding a server that is not yet running can leave a single-voter cluster with no leader, no commits and no in-band way back until that server runs or an operator recovers out of band. Alongside those sit five suspicions refuted with evidence rather than argument - the interrupted-transfer goroutine stranding, the stale TimeoutNow producer, the stronger stale-read readings for uniform clusters, the replication backoff, and the FSM-backpressure stall - plus one behaviour entry corrected under its own id with its affected use answered and one durable fact recording why the same blocking send is fatal at startup and merely delaying at runtime. Several of my own earlier readings were narrowed by their own receipts, and those narrowings remain in the record.\"}"}}
